---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Playground from '../components/Playground.astro';
const schema=[{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication',name:'Endpoint API Playground',applicationCategory:'DeveloperApplication',operatingSystem:'Web browser',url:new URL('/playground/',Astro.site).href,description:'A browser-only HTTP request editor with custom authentication, JSON tree, table, and raw response views.'}];
---
<Base title="API Playground — test HTTP requests in your browser" description="Send API requests directly from your browser with API keys, bearer tokens, or Basic authentication. Inspect JSON trees, tables, headers and raw responses." schema={schema}><main id="main" class="wrap playground-page"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>API playground</span></div><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">CURIOUS? MAKE A REQUEST.</span><h1>An API playground.<br/><em>All in your browser.</em></h1><p>Choose a documented example or bring your own endpoint. Edit, send, inspect—and take the code with you.</p></div><Playground/><section class="playground-help"><div><h2>Direct by design.</h2><p>Requests travel from your browser to the selected provider. Endpoint has no request proxy and does not receive or store your API credentials.</p></div><div><h2>Browser rules apply.</h2><p>The provider must allow cross-origin requests. A blocked request may still have reached the server; check its documentation before retrying a write.</p><a href="/guides/browser-api-requests-and-cors/">Understand CORS →</a></div><div><h2>Bring a test credential.</h2><p>Use a limited key or access token. Values remain in page memory and clear when you leave or reload. Code previews hide entered values by default.</p><a href="/guides/api-authentication/">Authentication explained →</a></div></section></main></Base>
